<title>LEBANON: Lebanon budget deficit 53.1 pct at end November.</title>
<headline>Lebanon budget deficit 53.1 pct at end November.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's budget deficit rose to 3,446 billion Lebanese pounds, or 53.1 percent, at the end of November, according to finance ministry statistics.</p>
<p>This compared with a planned deficit of revenue against expenditure of 2,428 billion pounds, or 37.6 percent, for the full year under the 1996 budget law.</p>
<p>Accumulated expenditures at the end of November were 6,487 billion pounds including debt servicing payments totalling 2,514 billion, and revenues were 3,041 billion.</p>
